WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.407 --> 00:00:04.111
CONTROVERSIAL FARM BILL

00:00:01.008 --> 00:00:04.545
SUPPORTED BY THE SPEAKER AND OF

00:00:04.245 --> 00:00:06.147
THE PRESIDENT.

00:00:04.678 --> 00:00:08.983
CHIEF CONGRESSIONAL

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.483
CORRESPONDENT MIKE EMANUEL SHOWS

00:00:09.116 --> 00:00:12.586
US WHAT HAPPENED.

00:00:09.617 --> 00:00:14.588
&gt;&gt; ON THIS BOAT THE EYES ARE 198

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.991
AND THE NAMES ARE TO 13.

00:00:14.722 --> 00:00:18.459
THE BILL DOES NOT PASS.

00:00:17.124 --> 00:00:20.594
&gt;&gt; Reporter: THEY DEFEATED A

00:00:18.592 --> 00:00:21.996
FIVE YEAR FARM BILL DEFINING

00:00:20.728 --> 00:00:22.463
G.O.P. LEADERS AND

00:00:22.129 --> 00:00:24.598
PRESIDENT TRUMP.

00:00:22.596 --> 00:00:25.399
THE CONSERVATIVES MINISTRY VOTE

00:00:24.732 --> 00:00:27.601
ON A SECURITY FOCUSED

00:00:25.533 --> 00:00:29.003
IMMIGRATION PLAN BEFORE THE FARM

00:00:27.735 --> 00:00:29.804
BILL, WITH SOME REPUBLICANS

00:00:29.136 --> 00:00:39.580
SIGNING ON WITH DEMOCRATS TO

00:00:29.937 --> 00:00:41.816
FORCE A VOTE ON ADDRESSING, DACA

00:00:39.713 --> 00:00:43.818
IT BECAME AN EMERGENCY.

00:00:41.949 --> 00:00:44.785
&gt;&gt; I WOULD SAY IT DOESN'T EXPIRE

00:00:43.951 --> 00:00:46.821
UNTIL SEPTEMBER SO WE HAVE

00:00:44.919 --> 00:00:48.789
PLENTY OF TIME TO DEAL WITH IT,

00:00:46.954 --> 00:00:49.590
BUT WE COULD BE DEALING WITH IT

00:00:48.923 --> 00:00:51.025
NEXT MONTH.

00:00:49.723 --> 00:00:51.792
SO IT'S MORE IMPORTANT RIGHT NOW

00:00:51.158 --> 00:00:55.996
TO PRIORITIZE IMMIGRATION AND WE

00:00:51.926 --> 00:00:56.397
HAVE BEEN ASKING AND WAITING FOR

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:57.097
MONTHS.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.666
&gt;&gt; Reporter: HOUSE G.O.P.

00:00:57.231 --> 00:01:00.401
LEADERS PUT THE FARM BILL ON THE

00:00:58.799 --> 00:01:01.602
FLOOR CALLING THEIR BLUFF.

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:03.637
THE PACKAGE INCLUDES POLICY

00:01:01.735 --> 00:01:05.206
CHANGES FAVORED BY THE PRESIDENT

00:01:03.771 --> 00:01:06.373
AND THE SPEAKER INCLUDING HAVING

00:01:05.339 --> 00:01:07.842
ABLE-BODIED FOOD STAMP

00:01:06.507 --> 00:01:08.409
RECIPIENTS WORK OR RECEIVE JOB

00:01:07.975 --> 00:01:09.877
TRAINING.

00:01:08.542 --> 00:01:12.246
THE BILL CAN BE BROUGHT UP AGAIN

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:13.981
WHEN THE LEADERSHIP IS CONFIDENT

00:01:12.379 --> 00:01:15.683
THEY HAVE A VOTE.

00:01:14.114 --> 00:01:16.684
&gt;&gt; SURE IT'S DISAPPOINTING, WE

00:01:15.816 --> 00:01:17.818
NEED TO MOVE FORWARD ON THE FARM

00:01:16.817 --> 00:01:19.620
BILL AND THE REPUBLICANS WANT TO

00:01:17.952 --> 00:01:20.521
MOVE FORWARD ON THE REFORM FOR

00:01:19.753 --> 00:01:23.891
THE FOOD STAMP PROGRAM.

00:01:20.654 --> 00:01:25.459
&gt;&gt; THE FOOD CAMP, EXAM PROGRAM

00:01:24.024 --> 00:01:25.826
KEPT THEM UNIFIED ON THE FARM

00:01:25.593 --> 00:01:27.261
BILL.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.996
TOP DEMOCRATS SAY EASING THE

00:01:27.394 --> 00:01:30.264
WORK REQUIREMENTS COULD HELP

00:01:29.129 --> 00:01:32.066
DELIVER VOTES FROM HIS SIDE.

00:01:30.397 --> 00:01:32.600
&gt;&gt; THE WHOLE PROBLEM WAS FOOD

00:01:32.199 --> 00:01:34.602
STAMPS.

00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:36.770
IT COULD HAVE BEEN WORKED OUT.

00:01:34.735 --> 00:01:39.006
I'M NOT HAPPY THAT THIS FAILED.

00:01:36.904 --> 00:01:40.174
YOU KNOW, I'M NOT HAPPY WE ARE

00:01:39.139 --> 00:01:41.909
IN THIS SITUATION, BUT I AM

00:01:40.307 --> 00:01:44.411
WILLING TO DO WHAT I CAN TO TRY

00:01:42.042 --> 00:01:45.379
TO FIX IT.

00:01:44.545 --> 00:01:46.413
&gt;&gt; Reporter: AT THE

00:01:45.512 --> 00:01:48.082
WHITE HOUSE SAYS THE PRESIDENT

